1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,470
Pip reads a ready-made mind map.

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,900
Basil makes his own, from memory.

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,590
One week later, who will remember more?

4
00:00:10,145 --> 00:00:12,345
I will read the poster five times.

5
00:00:12,555 --> 00:00:14,051
Reading feels safe!

6
00:00:14,071 --> 00:00:15,591
And I will make my own map.

7
00:00:15,691 --> 00:00:17,301
Let's see who remembers more!

8
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:19,660
Our Magnets quiz is next Monday.

9
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:22,040
Let's find out whose way works best!

10
00:00:22,315 --> 00:00:24,685
A little crow is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:24,945 --> 00:00:26,185
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:26,306 --> 00:00:28,946
Look up high, on the railings and the lamp posts!

13
00:00:28,996 --> 00:00:30,456
You against the Buddies!

14
00:00:30,726 --> 00:00:32,576
Lock in first with your fingers.

15
00:00:32,846 --> 00:00:34,676
One finger for every point.

16
00:00:35,257 --> 00:00:36,407
Today you'll learn:

17
00:00:36,609 --> 00:00:37,769
Make your own map.

18
00:00:37,971 --> 00:00:39,561
Work it out to remember it.

19
00:00:39,758 --> 00:00:40,938
Memory first.

20
00:00:41,441 --> 00:00:42,381
Are you ready?

21
00:00:42,821 --> 00:00:43,591
Three!

22
00:00:43,971 --> 00:00:44,631
Two!

23
00:00:45,001 --> 00:00:45,651
One!

24
00:00:46,071 --> 00:00:46,791
Go!

25
00:00:48,245 --> 00:00:50,185
Round one is a word puzzle.

26
00:00:50,435 --> 00:00:51,845
Play it with the Buddies!

27
00:00:51,977 --> 00:00:53,917
Read the three words on the left.

28
00:00:54,187 --> 00:00:56,807
On the right, three words have letters missing.

29
00:00:57,097 --> 00:00:58,187
Work them out!

30
00:01:03,275 --> 00:01:04,865
Repel, South and iron!

31
00:01:05,005 --> 00:01:06,475
I worked them all out!

32
00:01:06,679 --> 00:01:09,969
Later in this video, which words will you remember better?

33
00:01:10,269 --> 00:01:11,849
One, the words you read.

34
00:01:12,149 --> 00:01:14,019
Two, the words you worked out.

35
00:01:14,289 --> 00:01:15,719
Three, both the same.

36
00:01:16,009 --> 00:01:17,319
Show me your fingers!

37
00:01:22,792 --> 00:01:23,772
Locked in!

38
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:24,490
One.

39
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:27,650
The words on the left were clear and easy, so they will

40
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:28,920
stay in my head.

41
00:01:28,974 --> 00:01:29,494
Two.

42
00:01:29,794 --> 00:01:32,384
When I work out a riddle, I never forget it!

43
00:01:32,432 --> 00:01:33,072
Two!

44
00:01:33,232 --> 00:01:36,112
I had to think hard for those words, so my brain held

45
00:01:36,132 --> 00:01:37,092
on to them.

46
00:01:37,139 --> 00:01:38,809
We will test your memory later.

47
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:40,509
No scrolling back!

48
00:01:41,384 --> 00:01:42,534
Look closer.

49
00:01:43,094 --> 00:01:45,904
Pip reads the ready-made Magnets poster.

50
00:01:46,484 --> 00:01:49,996
His eyes slide along the branches, again and again.

51
00:01:50,016 --> 00:01:51,746
Basil makes his own map.

52
00:01:52,336 --> 00:01:55,876
He stops, he thinks, and he chooses his own words for every

53
00:01:55,896 --> 00:01:56,578
branch.

54
00:01:56,598 --> 00:02:00,228
Making your own map means you work out every branch yourself, such

55
00:02:00,248 --> 00:02:04,198
as Basil's Two poles branch, with North pole and South pole!

56
00:02:07,497 --> 00:02:08,787
Say it with me!

57
00:02:09,501 --> 00:02:12,421
A mind map you make yourself helps you remember more than a

58
00:02:12,441 --> 00:02:13,911
map you only read.

59
00:02:16,536 --> 00:02:18,216
Time for the memory test!

60
00:02:18,486 --> 00:02:21,806
Without looking back, say the six words from the right side of

61
00:02:21,826 --> 00:02:22,706
each card.

62
00:02:22,996 --> 00:02:23,756
Think!

63
00:02:28,406 --> 00:02:32,326
Look closer at what Pip remembered, and what Basil remembered.

64
00:02:35,898 --> 00:02:38,718
Did you remember more of the words you worked out?

65
00:02:39,298 --> 00:02:40,618
Many people do.

66
00:02:41,218 --> 00:02:46,318
Scientists have tested this many times, with grown-ups and with children, and

67
00:02:46,338 --> 00:02:48,708
the worked-out words are remembered better.

68
00:02:49,288 --> 00:02:50,768
So the answer is two!

69
00:02:51,358 --> 00:02:53,048
Did you show two fingers?

70
00:02:53,628 --> 00:02:55,035
Put one finger up!

71
00:02:55,055 --> 00:02:55,775
Oh!

72
00:02:56,035 --> 00:02:58,445
I still have repel, South and iron.

73
00:02:58,655 --> 00:03:01,645
But needle, a word I did not work out, is gone!

74
00:03:01,665 --> 00:03:03,535
Scientists have a name for this.

75
00:03:03,609 --> 00:03:07,269
The generation effect means you remember something better when you work it

76
00:03:07,289 --> 00:03:10,439
out yourself, such as the missing words in our puzzle!

77
00:03:13,669 --> 00:03:14,659
My turn!

78
00:03:14,809 --> 00:03:16,559
I'm making my own map too.

79
00:03:16,679 --> 00:03:19,949
I copy each branch from the poster, word for word.

80
00:03:20,073 --> 00:03:21,633
Something is not right.

81
00:03:21,903 --> 00:03:24,083
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

82
00:03:24,363 --> 00:03:25,323
Hold on!

83
00:03:30,736 --> 00:03:31,866
Arms crossed?

84
00:03:32,136 --> 00:03:33,346
One finger up!

85
00:03:33,398 --> 00:03:35,898
Momo, copying is not remembering.

86
00:03:36,018 --> 00:03:39,038
Close the poster first, and draw what you remember.

87
00:03:39,268 --> 00:03:40,678
Then you can check.

88
00:03:40,737 --> 00:03:44,137
Memory first means you draw your map from memory before you look,

89
00:03:44,157 --> 00:03:46,817
such as my map, with the poster closed!

90
00:03:47,622 --> 00:03:48,782
Say it with me!

91
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:52,600
Draw your map from memory first, with the poster closed.

92
00:03:55,078 --> 00:03:56,538
Show me your score hand!

93
00:03:56,818 --> 00:03:57,848
Two fingers?

94
00:03:58,128 --> 00:03:59,498
You beat the Buddies.

95
00:03:59,778 --> 00:04:00,778
High five!

96
00:04:01,356 --> 00:04:02,706
Did you spot the crow?

97
00:04:02,986 --> 00:04:05,916
It was on top of the letterboxes in the void deck!

98
00:04:06,056 --> 00:04:07,536
Here is a fun fact!

99
00:04:07,596 --> 00:04:10,196
Crows can remember a person's face for years.

100
00:04:10,326 --> 00:04:14,206
Scientists wore masks near crows, and years later, the crows still knew

101
00:04:14,226 --> 00:04:15,226
the masks!

102
00:04:15,348 --> 00:04:16,628
Tell someone at home!

103
00:04:17,357 --> 00:04:19,557
Let's read today's key words together!

104
00:04:19,847 --> 00:04:20,607
Ready?

105
00:04:20,894 --> 00:04:21,934
Make your own.

106
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:24,870
Generation effect.

107
00:04:26,741 --> 00:04:28,001
Memory first.

108
00:04:29,617 --> 00:04:30,557
Well done!

109
00:04:31,129 --> 00:04:34,674
Tonight, I will read the poster five times, all at once.

110
00:04:34,694 --> 00:04:37,714
And I will draw my map again from memory, on Tuesday and

111
00:04:37,734 --> 00:04:38,816
on Thursday.

112
00:04:38,836 --> 00:04:41,066
Next Monday, a blank page each.

113
00:04:41,336 --> 00:04:43,336
Who draws more of the Magnets map?

114
00:04:43,636 --> 00:04:44,516
One, Pip.

115
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:45,856
Two, Basil.

116
00:04:46,136 --> 00:04:47,556
Three, both the same.

117
00:04:47,846 --> 00:04:50,656
Lock in your answer, and find out in Part Two!

118
00:04:51,614 --> 00:04:52,715
Say it with us!

119
00:04:53,515 --> 00:04:54,265
Ready?

120
00:04:54,388 --> 00:04:55,048
One!

121
00:04:55,388 --> 00:04:56,088
two!

122
00:04:56,393 --> 00:04:57,568
Now you know!
